♪♪

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.676
Hey.
-Yo, yo, that dude

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.545
is not from Germany.
-Benny Greb?

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:48.181
-No, he's from Canarsie.
-Oh, really?

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.782
He's not? He's from Brooklyn?

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:51.584
-Brooklyn.
-Really?

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:52.886
-Yeah.
-You recognized him?

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.320
-I went to high school with him.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.754
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.754 --> 00:00:57.857
-So why do you think he's doing
this cover story?

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.258
-Yeah, I don't know
what he's doing.

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:00.994
He's running some type of scam,
I don't know.

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.095
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:04.530
Insurance or something,
I don't know.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.766
-It's so helpful when you're
here because I feel like you

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.567
have such a good eye
for scam artists.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:11.003
-Yeah. I used to be one.

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:12.205
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.472
Now that I think of it, Benny --

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:15.240
-Everybody thinking
I was a comedian.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.509
-Oh, really? So the --

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:21.548
[ Laughter ]
Very, very inter--

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.782
Now, Tracy,
I love to have you here

00:01:23.782 --> 00:01:25.418
to get your bounce on the news.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:28.421
We had midterms this week. I
know you're a bit of a politico.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.757
-Yeah.
-Did you stay up late?

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:33.959
Did you follow it all?
-It was a race, I mean,

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:36.562
it happened and then, like,
you don't know. I won.

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:37.797
-Oh.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.499
-I'm the king of New York.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.200
-King? I didn't even realize.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.903
-And I'm ruling over everything.
I'm ruling over Brooklyn.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.138
-Okay.
-Manhattan.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.105
-Okay.
-Queens.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.541
-Okay.
-And the Bronx.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.076
Everything except
for Staten Island.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:53.079
-Okay, gotcha.
-That's Wu-Tang's territory.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.914
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, okay.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.949
So you're king of four
out of the five boroughs.

00:01:56.949 --> 00:01:58.284
That's very exciting.
-Yes.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.619
And one of my first rulings,

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.887
I'm going to be the head coach
of the Giants.

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:03.222
-Really?

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:04.657
The Giants are actually doing
pretty well this year.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.792
-Yeah, I love them.
We're gladiators.

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:08.427
We're gladiators.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:10.362
You know what John Lennon
called New York City?

00:02:10.362 --> 00:02:12.098
-What did John Lennon --
-He called it Rome.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.099
-Oh, wow.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.566
-This is the center
of the universe.

00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:15.902
-Gotcha.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.704
-So this is exciting that you're
taking over --

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.305
You're the king of New York.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.407
You're taking over the Giants.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.442
Now, as a coach, what would be
the first rule

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:24.910
you would have as a coach
in the NFL?

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.146
-I would change the lunch.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:28.948
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.317
Everybody's eating
pork and beans and franks.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.518
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:34.687
Cowboy food.
-Yeah.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.789
Oh, that's very exciting.
You feel like maybe things have

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.259
gotten a little too nutritious,
and you go back to the old ways.

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:41.661
-Absolutely.
Whatever happened to knishes?

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:42.895
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:45.297
-That's true. You feel like --
-I love knishes.

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:46.365
-Uh-huh.

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:48.267
-I used to go to
Coney Island a lot.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.370
-To go have a knish?
-To have a knish.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.371
-There you go.
See, I find out new stuff

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:53.539
about you every time
you're here.

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:55.474
-You didn't know this about me?
-I didn't.

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.076
-All them years on
"Saturday Night Live,"

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.110
you didn't know I love knishes.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.312
-You kept this knish secret,
yeah.

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:03.382
Hey, I heard you're very
excited, I mean, I think we all

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:05.985
are about the new Black Panther
movie, "Wakanda Forever."

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.288
-Yeah, I auditioned for it.
-Oh, I'm sorry.

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:10.489
-I auditioned for "Black Adam."
-Really?

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.659
-I'll audition for anything
with the word "black" in it.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:16.629
[ Laughter ]
-Great.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:20.166
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.935
So what happened at the audition
for "Wakanda"?

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.504
-They didn't hire me.
-Okay.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:27.807
-They said I looked like
Garfield with my tights on.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.810
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.178
-They don't know what
they talking about.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:34.179
-That would work agai--
Yeah, I would say that maybe,

00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:36.615
but you'll still see it.
You're still excited to see it.

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:38.317
-How much you selling
that guitar for?

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:41.320
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.622
-Will you please stop trying to
buy my instruments?

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:46.192
-I need to buy the guitar!

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:49.362
If she ever got on crack,
she would sell that for $20.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.764
[ Laughter ]
-Oy, if there's ever a reason

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.533
